Firefox video on the overlay plane: translucent content over the video keeps it in software

On top of 0007 (docs/design/firefox-video-overlay.md §9.6). app_server shows
the plane only where the window holds the exact key colour, so a translucent
pixel over a planed video (a caption's background, text edges straight on the
video) blended with the key green, not with the picture. A1b's rule (software
while the content over the video changes) does not cover still content.
SwCompositor now checks the picture-cache tiles composited above the video
before it offers it to the plane: a tile being updated this frame, or one
with any pixel whose alpha is neither 0 nor 255 over the video's rect, keeps
the video in software. A tile's answer is kept until the tile changes
(invalidate_tile), so a still page scans its tiles once.

